  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree features smooth, mottled bark that peels away in patches, providing a visual example of bark exfoliation. Its long, narrow leaves can be used to discuss leaf shapes and adaptations to dry climates. The tree produces small, white flowers that attract various pollinators, making it a good subject for lessons on plant-pollinator interactions. The distinctive scent of its leaves can also be explored in discussions about plant chemistry and essential oils.",
